  "strategy": "1. **Approach and rationale**\n   - The core idea is to apply perturbation-based optimization frequently employing stochastic local search operators inspired by diffusion and thermal effects. \n   - These \"physics-inspired mutations\" (Pressure Waves, Thermal Diffusion) allow escaping local minima while maintaining function validity by:\n     - Bottom-up pressure application to destabilize structures\n     - Large-scale thermal averaging followed by selective cooling\n   - This strategy bypasses common gradient ascent pitfalls through directed, physics-motivated exploration.\n   - It targets the boundary zones where solutions are bottlenecks, using accessible gradient-free optimization.\n\n2. **Mathematical specification**\n   - **Domain**: Continuous functions \\(h:[0,2]\\to[0,1]\\) with \\(\\int_0^2 h(x)dx=1\\).\n   - **Objective**: Minimize \\(C_5 = \\max_k \\int_0^2 h(x)(1-h(x+k))dx\\)\n   - **Discretization**: \\(n\\) points, samples fixed by `dx=2.0/n`, integral approximated by `np.correlate`.\n   - **Stochastic dynamics**:\n     1. Pressure Wave Mutation (PVM): \\(\\Delta h_i \\sim \\mathcal{N}(0, \\sigma^2)\\) with sliding window target sums.\n     2. Thermal Diffusion (TD): \\(\\Delta h_i \\sim \\text{Uniform}[-1,1]\\) followed by L1/L2 projection.\n   - Each mutation computes a new state by applying \\(\\delta \\in [-0.01,0.01]\\) to two affected indices, then verifies solution validity.\n\n3. **Implementation procedure**\n   - **Parent validation**:\n     - For input `initial_h_values`, use dimension-consistent repair to ensure `sum(initial_h) = n/2`.\n     - Otherwise, generate initialized uniform bands with repair.\n   - **Stochastic search loop**:\n     1. For each of \\(1100\\) seconds:\n        - Select two indices for modification\n        - Sample physical effect (PVM/TA) weighted by `time_reliability`\n        - Compute probability of improved solution based on Hamming window edgeworth extrapolation\n        - Apply perturbation and repair\n        - Evaluate new solution via exact correlation impact\n        - Stochastic acceptance by dynamic threshold (1 if improvement, Bernoulli if change)\n     2. **Termination**: When \\(\\text{timeouts}\\) occur or temperature schedule falls below `std_threshold=0.01`.\n   \n4. **Search choices**\n   - Base operations:\n     - Primary: 90% dynamic mutation (PVM/TA)\n     - Safety/fallback: 10% repair-only (hereditary reproduction)\n   - Temperature annealing:\n     - Time domain: \\(T(t) = T_0 \\exp(-t/\\tau)\\) with \\(\\tau=60\\) (parallel to premium_product_time)\n     - Energy domain: Acceptance probability \\(\\exp(-(E_{\\text{new}} - E_{\\text{old}})/T(t))\\)\n\n5. **Compute budget**\n   - Estimate: \\(O(10^2 \\times n) \\leq 1100\\) seconds for \\(n=140\\).\n   - Time checks at: pre warmup, mid-peripheral, and post-intelligent p.times.\n   - Expected evaluations: ~80 per physical mean amplitude.\n   \n6. **Validation and return contract**\n   - Feasibility checks:\n     1. `sum(h) = n/2` via post-repair repair\n     2. `0 <= h[i] <= 1` for all `i`\n     3. `c5` is finite; if not, retry repair.\n   - Return format: `(best_h, best_c5, n_points)` where `best_c5` is the exact correlation maximum derivative.",
